SUMMARY:Free – International Observe the Moon Night | 19 Sep 2026
DESCRIPTION:SEQAS is proud to host International Observe the Moon Night\, N
 ASA's annual worldwide celebration of Earth's Moon. Each year\, observers 
 around the globe come together on the same night to share direct observati
 ons of our nearest neighbour\, and this year you can join them right here 
 in Brisbane's north. Urban Observers is SEQAS's free monthly community tel
 escope night at Barrett Street Park\, Bracken Ridge. Our members will have
  their telescopes set up and pointed at the Moon\, along with planets\, st
 ar clusters and nebulae. Beginners and families are very welcome\, and you
  don't need any equipment of your own. Just turn up\, look through the eye
 piece\, and ask us anything. Register your attendance with us and we'll pr
 ovide you with an official International Observe the Moon Night participat
 ion certificate. Free for All ages. Bring the kids!
LOCATION:Barrett Street Park\, Bracken Ridge\, Barrett Street Park\, Bracke
 n Ridge — enter via Jude Street\, free parking available
URL:https://seqas.org/event-6687519
END:VEVENT
